# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules: the reactor builds
# service's dependency from source (`configuration` is never published), and a module list would have
# to be edited every time a module is added. This file is what makes that cheap — it drops everything
# the build does not need, so adding a module stays free and no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage, and hundreds of megabytes of it
# here. Copying it in would also risk a stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# THERE IS NO CLIENT HERE, so this file carries none of the Quinoa-shaped exceptions its SPA-serving
# siblings do: no node_modules, no `.angular`, and above all no "do NOT exclude dist/" note. When a
# client arrives, copy that block from qits-events along with the rest of the recipe.

# Local env / IDE cruft. `.env` is per-machine Quarkus overrides read at ordinal 295 — above the
# packaged application.properties — so shipping one into the build context would let a developer's
# local value quietly outrank what the image is supposed to run with.
.env
.idea
.vscode
.settings
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing this Dockerfile does not bust the `COPY . .` layer. `configuration/` is a MODULE, not
# prose — it stays.
*.md
docs
docker
